# 02 — Naming Conventions

## File Naming

- All files: `kebab-case`.
- Files inside a type-folder follow `<name>.<folderName-singular>.ts`:
  - `user.service.ts`, `user.action.ts`, `user.validator.ts`, `user.type.ts`, `user.store.ts`
- Component files stay plain kebab-case: `user-avatar.tsx`.
- Next.js special files keep their required names: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts`, etc.

## General Naming Table

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files (general) | kebab-case | `user-profile.tsx` |
| Files (type-folders) | `name.folderName.ts` | `user.service.ts`, `user.action.ts` |
| Components | PascalCase | `UserProfile` |
| Functions/variables | camelCase | `getUserById` |
| Types | PascalCase | `User`, `CreateUserInput` |
| Zustand stores | camelCase, `use` prefix | `useCartStore` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE` |
| Zod schemas | camelCase, `Schema` suffix | `createUserSchema` |
| DB tables (Drizzle) | snake_case | `user_profiles` |
| Type guards | `is` prefix | `isUser`, `isProduct` |
| Env variables | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `DATABASE_URL` |
